cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use iri2026, please cite this software and the IRI model papers listed
  under "references". The IRI Working Group asks that any non-default JF switch
  settings be stated in publications.
type: software
title: "iri2026: IRI-2026 International Reference Ionosphere from Python"
version: 2026.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-16
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/xnchu/iri2026
authors:
  - family-names: Chu
    given-names: Xiangning
    email: xiangning.chu@lasp.colorado.edu
    affiliation: Laboratory for Atmospheric and Space Physics (LASP), University of Colorado Boulder
abstract: >-
  Python wrapper (build-on-run CMake, xarray API, command-line plotting scripts)
  around the IRI-2026 Fortran release of the International Reference Ionosphere.
  Derived from the iri2020 wrapper by Michael Hirsch and the space-physics
  organisation.
references:
  - type: article
    title: "The International Reference Ionosphere model: A review and description of an ionospheric benchmark"
    authors:
      - family-names: Bilitza
        given-names: Dieter
      - family-names: Pezzopane
        given-names: Michael
      - family-names: Truhlik
        given-names: Vladimir
      - family-names: Altadill
        given-names: David
      - family-names: Reinisch
        given-names: Bodo W.
      - family-names: Pignalberi
        given-names: Alessio
    journal: Reviews of Geophysics
    volume: 60
    issue: 4
    year: 2022
    doi: 10.1029/2022RG000792
  - type: software
    title: "IRI-2026 Fortran release"
    authors:
      - name: "Dieter Bilitza and the COSPAR/URSI IRI Working Group"
    url: https://irimodel.org/IRI-2026/
    year: 2026
  - type: software
    title: "iri2020: IRI2020 ionosphere model from Python and Matlab"
    authors:
      - family-names: Hirsch
        given-names: Michael
      - name: "space-physics organisation"
    url: https://github.com/space-physics/iri2020
    doi: 10.5281/zenodo.240895
